# AGENTS.md — {{ cluster_name }}

Instructions for any coding agent working in this repository. This file is the
entry point; `CLAUDE.md` imports it for Claude Code.

**Read [`.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md)
before making any change.** It is plain Markdown. It holds the workflow, the
invariants, the change-type decision tree and the pre-merge gates, and its
`references/` files hold the procedures. Claude Code invokes it through the
Skill tool; other agents read the files directly.

## Template first

This repository is one cluster of a shared platform. Inventory values,
addresses, the application estate and this cluster's documents stay here.
Anything generic goes upstream first: roles, CI job templates, Terraform
modules and vendored gates to weisssrv-lib, repository shape to
weisssrv-cluster-template, tenant-repository shape to weisssrv-app-template. A
generic change landed only here is drift. The skill's § Where the generic half
of a change goes has the detail.

